error[Z0401]: `correlation` needs at least two variables
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:15
  |
2 | f.correlation(x)
  |               ^ one variable
  |
  = help: name the variables as a list: `correlation([wage, educ, hours])`

error[Z0401]: `correlation` needs a Bool, Int or Float, but `s` is Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:15
  |
2 | f.correlation([x, s])
  |               ^^^^^^ a Str variable of f
  |
  = help: choose a Bool, Int or Float variable; `f.describe()` lists the types

error[Z0101]: no variable `z` in `f`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:15
  |
2 | f.correlation([x, z])
  |               ^^^^^^ not a variable of f
  |
  = help: did you mean `x`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"x"`

